## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates ability to design a CKNE-driven throttling system across a real-time, multi-tenant telemetry path, balancing SLA commitments with global health.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE health propagation across hops
- Per-tenant priority and budget management
- Minute-by-minute degradation policy and backpressure
- Payload schemas and validation
- Testing for bursts and SLA adherence

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo throttle by CKNE health (high level, not production-ready)
function throttleByCKNE(tenantId, ckne) {
  const bucket = getTenantBucket(tenantId);
  if (ckne.health < 0.5) bucket.reduce(ckne.sampling);
  // return true to emit, false to drop
  return Math.random() < bucket.sampling;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate correctness under micro-bursts with minimal data loss?
- How would you adapt this for multi-region deployments with cross-region CKNE signals?

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates ability to translate CKNE scores into concrete rate-limiting budgets with a testable rebalancing loop that preserves baseline SLA.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-based fairness and backpressure
- Per-tenant token buckets and sliding window rates
- Minute-granularity reallocation and SLA guarantees

## Code Example

```javascript
function computeShare(ckne) {
  const sum = ckne.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
  if (sum === 0) return ckne.map(()=>1/ckne.length);
  return ckne.map(v => Math.max(0.01, v / sum));
}
```

